= The Czechoslovak Revolt and Komuch

In late May, a Czechoslovak Legion of about 40,000 men, travelling east on the Trans-Siberian railway to rejoin the Allies, clashed with local Soviet authorities and took the towns along the line. On 8 June, in Samara, a group of SR members of the dissolved Constituent Assembly, under Vladimir Volsky, proclaimed a Committee of Members of the Constituent Assembly, Komuch, with the Legion's protection. It has declared itself the government of Russia, and is calling up an army.

It is the first anti-Bolshevik socialist government, and it is protected by foreign bayonets. Our Menshevik comrades in the Volga region are asked to join. Ivan Maisky, a Menshevik Internationalist, has gone to Samara and accepted a ministry. Most of the party leadership would say that it is a crime to cooperate with a force of interventionists; some say that it is a crime to refuse.

- @neither: "Neither side." Expel Maisky.
- @join: Join Komuch.
- @delegation: Send a delegation with a labour programme.

@neither
on-arrival: {!
Q.activists_strength = 4;
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: -4, rel_bol: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -3);
Q.maisky_expelled = 1;
!}

Maisky was expelled from the party. We have said that we are for neither side. It is a position that nobody on the Volga can understand.

@join
on-arrival: {!
Q.armed_struggle = 1;
Q.white_aid += 2;
Q.activists_strength = 12;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 10, rel_bol: -15, repression: 8, soviet_democracy: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 4, middle: 4, workers: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 4, -8);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -4, 20);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 10);
Q.members -= 12 * Q.mem_scale;
if (Q.legality > 1) { Q.legality -= 1; }
!}

A Menshevik delegation joined Komuch in Samara. The Bolsheviks have taken it as a declaration of war, and will treat our members in Moscow as hostages.

@delegation
on-arrival: {!
Q.white_aid += 0.5;
Q.activists_strength = 6;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 3, rel_bol: -6, repression: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 2, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
!}

A Menshevik delegation, led by Maisky's friends, has gone to Samara with a programme of workers' demands: restoration of the eight-hour day, trade union freedoms and no restoration of private estates. It is a middle position, and is attacked on both sides.
